{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788298458904,"sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_802e3e17058449cc8b0f2120","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 159"},"output":"title:\tRetire the three stdin keywords for one Stream<Str> source, parse(.) as a library call\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t159\n--\nRuling from the call-syntax-and-outside-world grill round (stdin-syntax-design board row), tentative per the maintainer's own hedge (\"not totally certain but I'm leaning towards this\"): **one Stream<Str> source, parse as a library call** -- retiring `input`, `inputs`, and `lines` for a single raw source (working name `stdin`), with today's `input`/`inputs` behavior expressed as an ordinary `parse(.)` call over it.\n\nShape ratified (from the round's preview, PROPOSED/unverified):\n\n```toylang\nfn total(nums: Vec<Int>) -> Int = length(nums)\ntotal(collect(stdin | map(parse(.))))\n```\n\nGiven the hedge, and given the round itself named \"verify type-flow's reach before deciding\" as a live alternative, the build for this (tracked as the existing stdin-redesign-build board row) should start with the smallest possible proof that `parse(.)` inside a `map` body actually resolves an expected type end-to-end -- the premise `type-flow-rework` (gh:44) was assumed, not directly re-verified, when this ruling was made.\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tRetire the three stdin keywords for one Stream<Str> source, parse(.) as a library call\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t159\n--\nRuling from the call-syntax-and-outside-world grill round (stdin-syntax-design board row), tentative per the maintainer's own hedge (\"not totally certain but I'm leaning towards this\"): **one Stream<Str> source, parse as a library call** -- retiring `input`, `inputs`, and `lines` for a single raw source (working name `stdin`), with today's `input`/`inputs` behavior expressed as an ordinary `parse(.)` call over it.\n\nShape ratified (from the round's preview, PROPOSED/unverified):\n\n```toylang\nfn total(nums: Vec<Int>) -> Int = length(nums)\ntotal(collect(stdin | map(parse(.))))\n```\n\nGiven the hedge, and given the round itself named \"verify type-flow's reach before deciding\" as a live alternative, the build for this (tracked as the existing stdin-redesign-build board row) should start with the smallest possible proof that `parse(.)` inside a `map` body actually resolves an expected type end-to-end -- the premise `type-flow-rework` (gh:44) was assumed, not directly re-verified, when this ruling was made.\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 159","time":{"start":1788298458896,"end":1788298458901}},"id":"prt_05ee4f3dd001gnuVQ4SrpCW9vV","sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","messageID":"msg_05ee4ea030016WT85CbEk51Kg3"}}
