{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788298461210,"sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_7456517699bb46e786681054","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git status"},"output":"On branch issue-159\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\tLAND-FAILURE.txt\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n","metadata":{"output":"On branch issue-159\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\tLAND-FAILURE.txt\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git status","time":{"start":1788298461205,"end":1788298461207}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me understand the situation. This is a language-design project. The issue #159 is about retiring the three stdin keywords (input, inputs, lines) for one Stream<Str> source, with parse(.) as a library call.\n\n A previous worker completed the task but the landing failed with merge conflicts with main. My job: merge origin/main into this branch, resolve conflicts in favor of intent (both sides' tests must still pass), fix whatever LAND-FAILURE.txt shows failing, and re-run the gate.\n\n Let me look at the current state of the repo.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ee4ffe5001HFzCGc46B0eDhY","sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","messageID":"msg_05ee4f73b001fD51C1Js4AV072"}}
