{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788298465834,"sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_d1c271608b89491b8072ca32","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git show --stat 45c76be"},"output":"commit 45c76bedb230aa116e19dbd1e30e47aee4ca4d94\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 23:26:58 2026 +0200\n\n    Retire input/inputs/lines for one stdin source with parse as a library call\n    \n    The stdin-syntax-design ruling (gh:159, tentative): three keywords become a\n    single raw Stream<Str> source named `stdin`, and reading a value is an\n    ordinary `parse(.)` call over it. The parser, checker, TIR, and every backend\n    now carry `stdin` and the `parse` builtin instead of the three source forms;\n    the host connects live stdin only when the program reads the source.\n    \n    Source migration only; the corpus and test files still spell the old keywords\n    and land in a follow-up.\n    \n    Human-authored: the single-source shape and parse-as-library-call semantics\n    Derived: per-backend parse emission from each target's native JSON handling\n    Agent-invented: the parse_read checked-form wiring in the checker\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode <git@daniel-kantor.com>\n\n build.rs               |   5 +-\n runtime/toylang.c      | 149 +++--------------------\n src/ast.rs             |  21 +---\n src/check/linearity.rs |  10 +-\n src/check/mod.rs       | 254 +++++++++++----------------------------\n src/emit_go.rs         | 127 ++++++++++----------\n src/emit_jq.rs         |  32 ++---\n src/emit_js.rs         |  43 ++-----\n src/emit_llvm.rs       | 114 ++++--------------\n src/emit_lua.rs        | 137 ++++++++++++++++------\n src/emit_py.rs         |  40 ++-----\n src/emit_rs.rs         | 120 ++++++-------------\n src/emit_toylang.rs    |   4 +-\n src/lib.rs             | 313 +++++++++----------------------------------------\n src/main.rs            |  24 +---\n src/parse.rs           |  18 +--\n src/tags.rs            |   9 +-\n src/tir.rs             |  43 +++----\n 18 files changed, 436 insertions(+), 1027 deletions(-)\n","metadata":{"output":"commit 45c76bedb230aa116e19dbd1e30e47aee4ca4d94\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 23:26:58 2026 +0200\n\n    Retire input/inputs/lines for one stdin source with parse as a library call\n    \n    The stdin-syntax-design ruling (gh:159, tentative): three keywords become a\n    single raw Stream<Str> source named `stdin`, and reading a value is an\n    ordinary `parse(.)` call over it. The parser, checker, TIR, and every backend\n    now carry `stdin` and the `parse` builtin instead of the three source forms;\n    the host connects live stdin only when the program reads the source.\n    \n    Source migration only; the corpus and test files still spell the old keywords\n    and land in a follow-up.\n    \n    Human-authored: the single-source shape and parse-as-library-call semantics\n    Derived: per-backend parse emission from each target's native JSON handling\n    Agent-invented: the parse_read checked-form wiring in the checker\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode <git@daniel-kantor.com>\n\n build.rs               |   5 +-\n runtime/toylang.c      | 149 +++--------------------\n src/ast.rs             |  21 +---\n src/check/linearity.rs |  10 +-\n src/check/mod.rs       | 254 +++++++++++----------------------------\n src/emit_go.rs         | 127 ++++++++++----------\n src/emit_jq.rs         |  32 ++---\n src/emit_js.rs         |  43 ++-----\n src/emit_llvm.rs       | 114 ++++--------------\n src/emit_lua.rs        | 137 ++++++++++++++++------\n src/emit_py.rs         |  40 ++-----\n src/emit_rs.rs         | 120 ++++++-------------\n src/emit_toylang.rs    |   4 +-\n src/lib.rs             | 313 +++++++++----------------------------------------\n src/main.rs            |  24 +---\n src/parse.rs           |  18 +--\n src/tags.rs            |   9 +-\n src/tir.rs             |  43 +++----\n 18 files changed, 436 insertions(+), 1027 deletions(-)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git show --stat 45c76be","time":{"start":1788298465831,"end":1788298465832}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So the branch HEAD is 45c76be (the issue-159 work), and the merge-base with origin/main is 7c4cc86. origin/main has advanced significantly since. The LAND-FAILURE.txt shows the merge attempt failed with conflicts in 15 files.\n\nMy job now: merge origin/main into this branch, resolve conflicts in favor of intent (both sides' tests must still pass), fix whatever LAND-FAILURE.txt shows failing, and re-run the gate.\n\n\n\nLet me first understand what the issue-159 commit changed. Let me look at the diff of commit 45c76be vs its parent 7c4cc86.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ee51204001rPjQ3hE5OQtdgu","sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","messageID":"msg_05ee50b60001HZtHMoGJt0GSE1"}}
