ames. Let me check.\n\n Hmm, but maybe I'm wrong. Let me look at the test suite and corpus. Also I should check whether the previous worker's branch actually passed `just check`. The task brief says: \"A previous worker completed this task, but landing the branch on main FAILED: merge conflict with main\". So the previous worker's implementation is complete on this branch. Presumably `just check` was green at the time. The corpus still spells old keywords? That seems contradictory...\n\nWait, let me re-read the commit message: \"Source migration only; the corpus and test files still spell the old keywords and land in a follow-up.\" Hmm, but that would break tests. Unless the checker/parser still accepts the old keywords as well as stdin? No, the diff clearly removed them from the token table.\n\n.\n\n Let me check the tests directory to see what's there.\n\n.\n\n Let me actually run `just check` to see the current state. But first, let me check what the corpus looks like.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ee56c770015REEQdrkrECWmv","sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","messageID":"msg_05ee54cf50015nvElNgirR1tXq"}}
