{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788298496426,"sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_29a3de4c0a4140d59fd61ab3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-159/tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_inputs.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-159/tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_inputs.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The one shape the compiler fuses into a read-one/transform-one/write-one loop instead of\n2: # reading all of stdin before printing anything: `jsonlines f inputs` where `f`'s own body is\n3: # a `map`/`select` chain over its parameter. Output is unaffected either way -- this case only\n4: # pins the value; tests/streaming.rs is what checks output actually arrives before stdin closes.\n5: program: |\n6:   fn adults(users: Stream<{name: Str, age: Int}>) -> Stream<{name: Str}> =\n7:       users | select(.age >= 18) | map {name: .name}\n8: \n9:   jsonlines adults inputs\n10: \n11: input: |\n12:   {\"name\": \"ada\", \"age\": 36}\n13:   {\"name\": \"bo\", \"age\": 9}\n14:   {\"name\": \"cy\", \"age\": 21}\n15: \n16: output: |\n17:   {\"name\":\"ada\"}\n18:   {\"name\":\"cy\"}\n19: \n20: node_types: [application, builtin.jsonlines, compare.ge, inputs, int, local, map-over, pipe, projection, record-literal, selection.narrow, var]\n\n(End of file - total 20 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The one shape the compiler fuses into a read-one/transform-one/write-one loop instead of\n# reading all of stdin before printing anything: `jsonlines f inputs` where `f`'s own body is\n# a `map`/`select` chain over its parameter. Output is unaffected either way -- this case only\n# pins the value; tests/streaming.rs is what checks output actually arrives before stdin closes.\nprogram: |\n  fn adults(users: Stream<{name: Str, age: Int}>) -> Stream<{name: Str}> =\n      users | select(.age >= 18) | map {name: .name}\n\n  jsonlines adults inputs\n\ninput: |\n  {\"name\": \"ada\", \"age\": 36}\n  {\"name\": \"bo\", \"age\": 9}\n  {\"name\": \"cy\", \"age\": 21}\n\noutput: |\n  {\"name\":\"ada\"}\n  {\"name\":\"cy\"}\n\nnode_types: [application, builtin.jsonlines, compare.ge, inputs, int, local, map-over, pipe, projection, record-literal, selection.narrow, var]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-159/tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_inputs.yaml","text":"# The one shape the compiler fuses into a read-one/transform-one/write-one loop instead of\n# reading all of stdin before printing anything: `jsonlines f inputs` where `f`'s own body is\n# a `map`/`select` chain over its parameter. Output is unaffected either way -- this case only\n# pins the value; tests/streaming.rs is what checks output actually arrives before stdin closes.\nprogram: |\n  fn adults(users: Stream<{name: Str, age: Int}>) -> Stream<{name: Str}> =\n      users | select(.age >= 18) | map {name: .name}\n\n  jsonlines adults inputs\n\ninput: |\n  {\"name\": \"ada\", \"age\": 36}\n  {\"name\": \"bo\", \"age\": 9}\n  {\"name\": \"cy\", \"age\": 21}\n\noutput: |\n  {\"name\":\"ada\"}\n  {\"name\":\"cy\"}\n\nnode_types: [application, builtin.jsonlines, compare.ge, inputs, int, local, map-over, pipe, projection, record-literal, selection.narrow, var]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":20,"totalLines":20,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_inputs.yaml","time":{"start":1788298496408,"end":1788298496425}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting! Some corpus files use `stdin` already. So the corpus was partially migrated. Let me check whether `just check` passes on the current branch. That would tell me whether the previous worker left it green.\n\nAlso I should check whether there were follow-up commits that migrated the corpus. Wait, HEAD is 45c76be. There's only one commit on the branch above the merge base (7c4cc86). The commit message says corpus migration lands in a follow-up. But some corpus files use stdin already — those might be files that got touched by the commit? Hmm. Let me check the commit diff for tests/... Actually, git show 45c76be --stat didn't show tests/. So the commit did NOT touch tests/. But some corpus files already have `stdin`. That means those were already using stdin... wait, that can't be, stdin didn't exist before. Unless upstream (main) already migrated some corpus files? Let me check: does main have stdin keyword support? No. Let me check the state of tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_inputs.yaml on the merge base and on main.\n\nActually wait. Let me look at what `stdin` appears in these files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ee58977001RDEobspZ51JGs6","sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","messageID":"msg_05ee579f20018sXX6Ce5dVb52e"}}
