{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788298508606,"sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_d906ae4fc6d4457ca6e8fce1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"Input|Inputs|Lines|Stdin\" src/parse.rs | head -20"},"output":"16:type Input<'i> = LocatingSlice<&'i str>;\n23:impl<'i> ParserError<Input<'i>> for Error {\n26:    fn from_input(input: &Input<'i>) -> Error {\n47:    Stdin,\n90:            Tok::Stdin => \"`stdin`\",\n126:fn skip_trivia(input: &mut Input) {\n145:fn read_tok<'i>(input: &mut Input<'i>) -> Result<(Tok, Span), Error> {\n178:                \"stdin\" => Tok::Stdin,\n251:fn single(input: &mut Input, tok: Tok) -> Tok {\n258:fn read_string(input: &mut Input) -> Result<String, Error> {\n436:    input: Input<'i>,\n457:    /// Reads the next token without consuming it. `Input` is `Copy` (a source `&str` plus an\n1162:            Tok::Str(_) | Tok::Int(_) | Tok::Stdin | Tok::Ident(_) => {\n1209:            Tok::Stdin => Ok(Expr::Stdin { span }),\n","metadata":{"output":"16:type Input<'i> = LocatingSlice<&'i str>;\n23:impl<'i> ParserError<Input<'i>> for Error {\n26:    fn from_input(input: &Input<'i>) -> Error {\n47:    Stdin,\n90:            Tok::Stdin => \"`stdin`\",\n126:fn skip_trivia(input: &mut Input) {\n145:fn read_tok<'i>(input: &mut Input<'i>) -> Result<(Tok, Span), Error> {\n178:                \"stdin\" => Tok::Stdin,\n251:fn single(input: &mut Input, tok: Tok) -> Tok {\n258:fn read_string(input: &mut Input) -> Result<String, Error> {\n436:    input: Input<'i>,\n457:    /// Reads the next token without consuming it. `Input` is `Copy` (a source `&str` plus an\n1162:            Tok::Str(_) | Tok::Int(_) | Tok::Stdin | Tok::Ident(_) => {\n1209:            Tok::Stdin => Ok(Expr::Stdin { span }),\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"Input|Inputs|Lines|Stdin\" src/parse.rs | head -20","time":{"start":1788298508602,"end":1788298508605}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So `just check` runs `cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'` — the docs mega-test is skipped but everything else runs, including corpus tests. If the corpus still has old keywords, then corpus tests would fail to parse.\n\n. Unless the corpus tests don't exist or the corpus files were migrated on the branch? But we saw input_typed_by_first_use.yaml still uses `input`. And it's in the working tree (clean, on branch). So on the branch HEAD, that file uses `input`, and the parser rejects it. So `just check` should fail.\n\n.\n\nBut the task says \"A previous worker completed this task\" — maybe the previous worker actually did NOT have `just check` green? Or maybe I'm wrong that the parser rejects old keywords. Let me verify: check src/parse.rs on the branch — does it still have Tok::Input? No, we saw the diff removed it. Let me actually read src/parse.rs current state.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ee5b92c001VesZcOy5U0D4Jo","sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","messageID":"msg_05ee5ad1b0014xPXFT1nQ5fPCK"}}
