edit (dropping If/Else) aligns with main. \n\nBut wait — is that really right? Could main still have if/else support somewhere else? No — main's Tok enum has no If/Else. So the language on main has no if/else keyword. Actually that's plausible: they redesigned conditionals around `cond`/`match`. Indeed the corpus has cond_branches_from_annotation.yaml etc.\n\n \n\nSo my edit produced:\n```\nEnum,\n    Let,\n    Stdin,\n    Dsv,\n    Csv,\n    Tsv,\n```\n\nBut hold on — I need to double check that If/Else really were removed by main and not just moved. Let me search main's parse.rs for \"if\" keywords.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ee6983d001NSQrNA30UmNN34","sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","messageID":"msg_05ee67e8e001au8q7uVtyEs888"}}
