{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788298595286,"sessionID":"ses_fa11b16e3ffejSNgKGkK0vX2sJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_cd66db73ca3b48d0b501d7db","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-159/src/tir.rs","limit":80,"offset":30},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-159/src/tir.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n30:     VecLit(Vec<Tir>),\n31:     /// A record literal, its fields in declaration order so a field's position here matches\n32:     /// its position in the type. That is what lets a backend address one by index rather than\n33:     /// searching for it.\n34:     RecordLit {\n35:         fields: Vec<(String, Tir)>,\n36:     },\n37:     /// A constructed enum value. The node's type is the enum, so a backend finds the variant's\n38:     /// position (its tag, where one is needed) and its payload type by asking `ty::variants`\n39:     /// for that type's list rather than by carrying either here. `payload` is `None` for a unit\n40:     /// variant, which every backend renders as the bare variant-name string; a payload variant\n41:     /// is the single-key wrapper (ADR 0009).\n42:     EnumLit {\n43:         variant: String,\n44:         payload: Option<Box<Tir>>,\n45:     },\n46:     /// Rebuilds an Opt: present-preserving, absent-preserving. `body` runs with `param` bound\n47:     /// to the unwrapped payload only when `source` is present; an absent `source` passes\n48:     /// through untouched. Never surface syntax -- Opt has no general map or match a program can\n49:     /// reach (kantord/toylang#47's totality round owns that) -- this is only how the checker's\n50:     /// own reorder pass reaches inside an Opt payload (kantord/toylang#66): every other enum\n51:     /// reorders through `Match`/`EnumLit`, but Opt keeps a representation of its own in three\n52:     /// backends, so those two general nodes cannot reach it.\n53:     OptMap {\n54:         